LOG="bash $HOME/.claude/skills/pstack/skills/show-me-your-work/scripts/log.sh"
T="$1"
$LOG $T sweep "Break StyleX equal-priority ties by value text" "StyleX sorts same-priority rules with localeCompare on the value, so source order would pick the wrong press transition" "press transition diff in the matrix went to 0 after the tie break; force-one 0 mismatches of 3186 targets" "kept in the codemod"
$LOG $T sweep "Carry comments through regeneration with a restoration lever" "The codemod regenerates src, so hand-restored comments would be lost on the next run" "lever comments.py in the record-levers commit; about 1000 comments moved unchanged" "kept"
$LOG $T sequence "Freeze the codemod sweep into one commit, then clean up as ordinary commits" "Once the sweep is frozen, each cleanup can be read and verified alone instead of hiding in a regenerated diff" "history shows the migrate commit followed by nine cleanup commits" "done"
$LOG $T migrate "Commit the levers under docs, then remove them in the removal commit" "A reviewer can rerun them from history while the merged tree carries no migration scaffolding" "record-levers commit holds them, about 3.7 MB; removal commit deletes docs/vanilla-extract-migration" "kept, droppable by the user"
$LOG $T bundle "Apply serverOwnsCss at build only" "With the plugin on in dev, astro dev rendered unstyled pages" "devcheck showed unstyled dev pages, styled after apply build; 5 versus 64 style elements in dev is per-module injection" "fixed"
$LOG $T verify "Force pseudo states over CDP and report the button-publish span as unreachable" "Forced focus-visible on a non-focusable span cannot happen to a user, so fixing it would chase the harness" "lab run2 421150 comparisons, 760 mismatches from 2 keys; src/rules/button-publish.astro:23" "reported, no fix"
$LOG $T verify "Compare motion signatures against the union of base control runs" "Base versus base differs by timing and canvas hash, so a pairwise diff measures noise" "motion-final 36 and motion-final2 19 signatures outside the union, 4 reproduce, each checked" "method kept"
$LOG $T verify "Mutation test the harnesses" "A harness reporting 0 proves nothing unless it can fail" "press transition-duration, breakpoint moved from 960 to 901, keyframe edits all flagged; unmutated 0" "harnesses trusted"
$LOG $T verify "Report design PDF size as a race that predates the migration" "PDF size varies between builds of the same tree through masked image timing" "base builds 393501 to 399529 bytes; text identical; 7 pages at 150 dpi byte-identical PNGs" "reported"
$LOG $T simplify "Fix the view-module and class-prop folds, skip duplication already at the base and CSS pruning" "Those skips are outside the migration wave and would change output the baselines pin" "skip list carried into the final report" "reported"
$LOG $T perf "State the claim first and serve base, control and new with the same server" "A control equal to base shows how much of a delta is noise" "240 rows and 120 trace rows, 0 errors; control medians within 2.2 percent of base on charted metrics" "method kept"
$LOG $T perf "Name throttled-link bytes as the limiter of the phone first paint gain" "The gain should follow from the byte delta or the claim is unexplained" "/cv Brotli delta 25163 B at 1.6 Mbps is 126 ms of the 166 ms gain, about 10 ms parse and 6 ms recalc" "accepted"
$LOG $T perf "Measure build time with 6 interleaved cold builds through gate-slot" "Interleaving cancels machine load drift, and removing caches measures the transform cost" "StyleX median 9.33 s, vanilla-extract 3.18 s; output checked against both reference builds" "reported"
$LOG $T verify "Finish the interrupted history rewrite and compare the tree" "A chained script ran on past a cherry-pick conflict and deleted its safety branch; the old commits stayed reachable through the reflog" "git diff 8ef11e5 against the result was empty" "recovered"
$LOG $T verify "Report modulepreload tag order as not caused by the migration" "Build output looked different from the reference on 10 pages, so the parity claim needed an explanation" "preload-cmp: base1 vs base2 13 raw 0 normalized; new1 vs new2 13 raw 0 normalized" "reported"
$LOG $T sequence "Fold the css-order typecheck fix into the test commit" "A per-commit run showed 4 commits failing typecheck, and each commit should pass on its own" "per-commit run over bd07ab6 to HEAD" "done"
